WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.780
Father Marcus asked me to

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.060
to speak a little bit about

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.080
the icons of the nativity of the mother of God and

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.400
to be honest, I–

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.100
to be honest [laughing]

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.120
[unintelligible]

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.140
to be, to be honest, um

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.440
I felt like the icon of the nativity of the mother of God is quite straightforward

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.520
if you look at it

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.220
you pretty much can understand what is going on

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.920
and so I thought I'd rather want to

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.120
propose a few thoughts about the very feast

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.320
that we're celebrating.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.120
The fact that our liturgical year starts with

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.060
this celebration of the birth

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.640
of the mother of God and then ends

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.380
with her falling asleep and, um…

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:58.080
It was great to hear the readings today,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.840
and to hear this reading from Genesis

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.020
and this idea of the house of God

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:07.360
which reading that you heard, um

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.840
from Ezekiel, this closed gate

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.040
and also the proverb, the house of wisdom

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.500
and what should we see in the um

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.500
in the reading of the song

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.140
all that we're hearing about is

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.400
this notion of the sacred place

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.920
of this, this holy place

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.280
that is there, that is prepared

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.040
that is built

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.680
that is ready to receive the Lord.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.780
In the book of Genesis we…

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.280
one of the things that happens at the Fall

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.100
is that God curses the Earth.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.420
He curses the ground.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.020
And in the Bible, the Old Testament

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.860
we see this idea that the ground is cursed

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.420
reappear in different ways.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.060
And one of the ways in which

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.580
it appears is this image

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.160
of the barren woman

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.980
that we find in the Old Testament

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.280
over and over.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.880
Sarah, Rachel,

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.960
we have this image of the barren woman.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.880
So a lot of times, people

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.720
you know, especially Protestants

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.040
they wonder a lot about things like

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.960
the feast of the Nativity of the Mother of God

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.100
or these traditions that have been

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.300
gathered from extrabiblical material

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.780
to talk about the life of the mother of God

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.100
But once we understand

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.460
the pattern of scripture

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.360
and we see this image of the barren woman

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.240
we understand that this part

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.100
this notion, this story

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.300
of Saint Anne

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.640
this barren woman

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.300
who gives birth to the pure virgin

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.580
That's one of the stories

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.040
that is there from the beginning of scripture

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.220
and follows all the way through

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.220
into the New Testament.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.440
One of the most

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.940
one of the most, um

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.100
One of the most, let's say

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.080
visible examples of that…

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.160
is when the Hebrews are in the desert

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.600
and they encounter the bitter waters.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.500
They encounter these waters

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.600
that cannot—that you can't drink.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.680
Bitterness is related to barrenness.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.320
There's even another place

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.040
in the Old Testament

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.860
where a woman who's lost all her children

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.240
says "now call me Bitter

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.240
it has become my name".

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.600
This notion of waters that aren't useful

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.780
that can't—that aren't productive of life

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.280
and the encounter of those bitter waters

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.880
with the tree

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.200
is what produces the sweet waters.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.160
What produces the pure waters.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.860
So we hear it in the song

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.240
if you listen to the uh

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.160
if you listen to the choir sing

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.360
you heard it said

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.740
our very nature

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.460
God has healed

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.460
has set aside our barren nature

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.020
because this story

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.840
even the story of the liturgical year

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.500
we always have to remember

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.640
that it's talking about us!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.380
That it's also talking about us.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.380
Right? We are also that barren land.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.980
We are also that barren woman.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.740
And through prayer

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.360
through faith

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.960
is how we are called.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.420
We're all called

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.420
to become the other woman.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.740
We're all called to become

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.080
the pure woman.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.780
So this transition that we see

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.120
in the story of St Anne

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.240
who gives birth to the virgin

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.300
That's the return into the garden

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.400
Moving out of the barren land

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:31.180
entering into that holy place

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.840
and that's why the mother of God

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.640
even in her story as a child

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.160
is always being related

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.080
to the holy place of the temple.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.200
She's mending the veil of the temple.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.600
She's secretly hidden in the holy place.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.460
'Cause that's who she is!

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.760
She is that holy place.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.100
And so,

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.800
even though we, like I said

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.340
if we understand the spirit of the scripture

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.980
and we see that pattern in the scripture

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.020
and we understand that

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.020
this transition from

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.020
the barren woman

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.320
that we've seen so many times

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.360
in the Old Testament

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.700
who gives birth to the pure woman

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.720
who then becomes the holy place

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.300
it is completely

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.820
It is, it is one of those fulfillments.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.400
One of those places where

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.540
you see the whole puzzle of the Fall

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.600
and the problem that it brought about

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.720
fulfill itself in the life of

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.760
the mother of God

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.300
as she becomes the place of our Lord.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.100
And so that is why

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.800
in the liturgical year we start

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.400
with that preparation.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.820
We start with that opening up

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.040
of the gates

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.620
the top of the garden

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.160
this holy place

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:41.900
And that's, like I said, that's us.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.680
That's what–we have to become that.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.840
We have to prepare ourselves.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.980
We have to, we have to, ah…

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.600
We have to build the house of God in our souls

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:56.340
so that we can have that encounter with our Lord.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.500
And so, those are the—

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.860
that little thought that I wanted to, uh

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.120
to give you today.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.800
Especially, and like I said

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.760
we live in North America

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.760
and we're surrounded by Bible-believing

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.760
Christians, um…

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.500
But once we, like I said

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.120
once we see that pattern in scripture

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.240
just how much it repeats itself

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.480
we can understand why the church has brought in

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.580
this extrabiblical tradition:

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.280
because it fits.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.300
It's helping us see

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:27.160
what exactly this is all about.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.580
What is this story about?

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.820
So, thank you for your time.

